new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9ce979e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/games/botw/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,90 @@
+# BOTW (work in progress)
+
+Native Apple-silicon port of The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild, following the same route as `../totk`
+(see the `ns-game-apple-arm-port` skill). Nothing from the game is stored here. Generated data lives outside the
+repository (see the project `AGENTS.md`).
+
+## Status
+
+The game boots and renders its opening (see First runs). The rest of this section covers extraction, rewriting and compile/link.
+
+- Version 1.9.0 is identified from verified ExeFS hashes (`versions.json`), not from file names.
+- `scripts/extract_exefs.py` reads the 1.9.0 update NSP in place and verifies the ExeFS hash blocks. It matches an
+  independent hactool extraction.
+- `sdk` and `subsdk0` are byte-identical to TOTK 1.4.3, and so are their rewrites. The NPDM lists the same 49 services.
+  Only `main` is BOTW-specific.
+- `main` rewrites with `third_party/d2r/patch_nso.py` after three BOTW-only signed jump tables were registered
+  (build ID `cd57b23fa4bbad65803d9788c01821ee`, sites `0x37df10`, `0x37ee84`, `0x37fdbc`). TOTK's `main` output is unchanged.
+- `scripts/prepare_runtime.py --version v190 --data-root <dir>` and `scripts/prepare_romfs_backend.py --version v190 --data-root <dir>`
+  generate the runtime tables and RomFS config outside the repository. The TOTK v143 outputs are byte-identical.
+- `runtime/game_patches_v190.c` is a baseline with no game patches (shipping speed and output size) and
+  `game_version.h` has a `TOTK_GAME_V190` branch whose TOTK addresses are sentinels, so any use fails loudly.
+- `scripts/build_native.sh <data-root> <output-dir> <fonts-config-dir>` compiles and links `botw-native-v190` outside the
+  repository. It has not been executed.
+
+## Known defect in the RomFS used so far
+
+The RomFS built from the available base game and 1.9.0 update does not pass the IVFC integrity check. The base game
+alone verifies cleanly (880,128 blocks, 0 bad; its Program NCA hash matches its name). The merged image has exactly one
+bad 1 MiB region (65 blocks), and every bad block comes from the update package: update NSP file offset
+`0x86fe990`-`0x8802990`. It lies inside one file, `Sound/Resource/Stream/Event_BGM_CompleteMasterSword.bfstm`, about
+82 % of it. The other 41,061 files verify. The update's Program NCA hash also does not match its file name.
+
+The image is marked `UNVERIFIED` in its folder. The runtime's own RomFS check compares the image against its own hash, so
+it cannot detect this. Replace the update package with a clean copy and rebuild before treating any result as final.
+
+## First runs (macOS, Apple M1 Max)
+
+All runs used the RomFS above and a data tree outside the repository. Evidence is local logs, not a finished port.
+
+- `probe` passes: three rewritten modules load, 223,994 relative relocations apply, 4,000 cross-module clock calls on 4 threads.
+- `probe-fs` passes on the unverified RomFS (41,062 files; its integrity check compares the image to its own hash and
+  cannot see the damaged 1 MiB). `probe-gpu-blockrt`, `probe-gpu-midclear` and `probe-gpu-widen` pass, which opens the
+  matching `TOTK_GPU_*` gates the game now needs.
+- `boot` runs the game's own startup: `nnosInitialize`, SDK startup, all constructors (`main` 1040, `subsdk0` 45, `sdk` 83),
+  `nnMain`, a window, DualSense input, audio output, and several thousand frames of rendering with real shader translation.
+- Magenta frame fixed (2026-10-20): BOTW never calls `nvnDeviceSetDepthMode` and relies on NVN's default,
+  `NEAR_IS_MINUS_W` (enum 0). The runtime's flag `g_depth_near_minus_w` (`hle_nvn.c`) started at 0, so BOTW's vertex
+  shaders were translated without the GL -> Metal clip-z conversion. TOTK is not affected because it sets the same mode
+  explicitly. `nvnDeviceInitialize` now sets the NVN default. With the fix the window shows the opening light flare
+  at 20 s and Link lying in the Shrine of Resurrection at 75 s (screenshots outside the repository).
+  How it was found: the last draw of every frame is a full-screen quad (vertices +-0.5, u16 indices 0,2,1,1,2,3) into the
+  swapchain texture. Its vertex shader multiplies by a constant buffer matrix that scales x and y by 2 and sets **z = -1**.
+  Metal clips z < 0, so the whole quad was discarded and the swapchain texture kept its initial 255,0,255. The evidence:
+  the draw is encoded every frame with no skip counter, and its indices are correct on the CPU side and also when copied
+  into the arena. A runtime-owned full-screen green triangle encoded in the same pass lands at 100 %. The grid VS
+  (`TOTK_GPU_HILITE_VS=1`, no inputs) with a solid fragment shader lands its tile, but the game's own VS does not.
+  **Translated shader variants are not keyed on the depth flag** (`totk_shader_rt.m`: the variant hash covers only the
+  answers). So a BOTW shader cache made before this fix keeps the unconverted vertex shaders. Delete it, or point
+  `TOTK_SHADER_CACHE` at an empty directory. The verification run used a fresh cache.
+  Ruled out on the way (kept for reference): window occlusion, missing RomFS files, shader translation failures, face
+  culling and winding, the render-encode thread, the sRGB view (`fmt 71` over `fmt 70`) of the swapchain texture, and the
+  present path. A TOTK control run on the same Mac rendered correctly.
+- Still open after the fix: the shrine scene is very dark and Link looks like a flat silhouette, so lighting or
+  material passes may still be wrong. The scene buffer that looked uniformly cream earlier is the opening flash.
+- Host calls BOTW makes that TOTK never did were added as local implementations: seven-six-axis sensor lifecycle (no
+  samples), `SetGyroscopeZeroDriftMode`, `SetNpadJoyAssignmentModeDual`, the one-argument `ShowControllerSupport`,
+  `IAudioRenderer` commands 12/13 (voice drop parameter), `nn::account::ListAllUsers`, `nn::fs::CommitSaveData`,
+  `nn::pl::IsRunningOnOunce` (reports not Switch 2), `IsVrMode`/`EndVrMode`/`BeginVrMode` (Begin stops loudly) and
+  `nn::oe::EnableRecording`. Controls the host cannot provide report that plainly.
+- Reserving the guest address space fails about one run in three on this Mac when the window is created at the same time.
+  `services.c` has someone else's uncommitted work on exactly this, so it was not touched; `TOTK_ALIAS_GIB=12` was used.
+- The runtime looks for its helpers under `<parent of the executable's folder>/build/`: `shader-service/totk_xlate` (the
+  checked-in prebuilt) and `spirv-cross/spirv-cross` (built by `build_app.py`).
+
+## Not done
+
+- BOTW-specific game patches: frame rate and output size. TOTK's adaptive present-interval patches have no counterpart
+  in BOTW's `main`. The present interval is read from a config field (`this+0xa0`, `main+0xe93dbc`), and the frame budget
+  is `(interval + 0.02) / 60` seconds (`main+0xe93df4`). Where the default of 2 is set, and whether game logic follows
+  measured frame time, is unknown.
+- Replacements for TOTK's loader checkpoints, the keyboard PLT/GOT offsets and the save-load crash workaround.
+- Shader seed, app bundle, signing, launcher, gamepad checks, and any run of the game.
+
+## Extract
+
+```sh
+python3 games/botw/scripts/extract_exefs.py <BOTW 1.9.0 update.nsp> --keys <prod.keys> --update --output <dir outside the repo>/exefs
+```
+
+The output directory must not exist yet.
